    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d562">

                <pb facs="0719" n="595" xml:id="pg595"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2176: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harvey</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-07-25T13:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 25, 1921—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 25—12:07
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>611. Your telegrams 405, July 15, 5 [<hi rendition="#italic">6</hi>] p.m. and
                    407, July 16, 1 p.m.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d562-f1"/> Foreign Office states that
                    British Minister at Peking has been instructed in the event of the question of
                    the bond issue being raised again by the Chinese Minister of Communications to
                    support view of the United States Government as laid down in memorandum handed
                    to the Chinese Minister at Washington on July 14, 1921.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harvey</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
